From: dotlouis <1891109+dotlouis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:07:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/41] MTROPOLIS: Load variable files from the game directory

The Save and Restore modifier is used by some games (e.g. Uncle Albert's
Fabulous Voyage) to load data files shipped with the game, which are
stored in the native mTropolis variable file format. When no ScummVM
save exists for a named load, parse the file from the project directory
and copy its values into the target variable. Saves still go to the
ScummVM save system and take precedence on later loads.

Also support vector values in plug-in data, read list values from
variable files even if the persistent flag is clear, and drop list
values that failed to load instead of using them uninitialized.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
